  "lead_raw_text": " The structure of Rb4In2Au2 (reduced formula Rb2InAu) crystallizes in the tetragonal space group I-4m2 (No. 119), with eight atoms per unit cell distributed over four independent Wyckoff orbits. Geometry-derived coordination analysis shows Au and In each surrounded by eight Rb neighbors, while Rb adopts two distinct environments: a 12-neighbor arrangement with four Au and eight Rb, and an eight-neighbor environment with four Au and four In. The periodic neighbor graph forms a single three-dimensional component spanning all eight sites. Validated polyhedron-sharing relations include corner-, edge-, and face-sharing between Au- and In-centered 8-vertex polyhedra, and corner- and edge-sharing between Au- or In-centered and Rb-centered 12-vertex polyhedra.\n<CRYSTAL_START>",
